Chromium Embedded Framework for Debian
=======================================

EXPERIMENTAL STATUS
-------------------

This package is EXPERIMENTAL and targeted for unstable/testing only.
It is NOT intended for stable releases at this time.

Binary Packages
---------------

This source package produces four binary packages:

  libcef145        - CEF shared library (libcef.so.145)
                     The version number (145) is the CEF major version.
                     See "CEF and Chromium Version Alignment" section below.

  libcef145-dbgsym - Debug symbols for libcef145 (auto-generated)

  libcef-dev       - Development files (headers, CMake configuration)
                     Depends on libcef145

  cef-common       - Architecture-independent data files (PAK files, locales)
                     Required at runtime by CEF applications

Source Package Structure (MUT)
------------------------------

This package uses Multiple Upstream Tarballs (MUT) format. All components
are distributed as separate tarballs and automatically extracted by
dpkg-source:

  orig.tar.xz           - CEF source code (main tarball)
  orig-chromium.tar.xz  - Chromium browser source
  orig-depot-tools.tar.xz - Google's depot_tools build system

When extracted with `dpkg-source -x`, these create:

  chromium-embedded-framework-VERSION/
  ├── cef/           <- CEF source
  ├── chromium/      <- Chromium source
  ├── depot-tools/   <- Google's build tools
  └── debian/        <- Packaging files

**No manual setup required** - all components are included in the source
package. See debian/README.source for detailed MUT documentation.

**Note on Bundled Components:**

These components are bundled as MUT tarballs as an interim solution:

  - chromium: Will migrate to chromium-source package when Bug #893448
    is resolved. This will allow automatic version tracking with Debian's
    Chromium security updates.

  - depot-tools: Could migrate to a Debian package if one is ever created.
    Currently bundled because depot_tools has no stable releases and
    requires specific commit alignment with Chromium versions.

Build Instructions
------------------

Standard build from source package:

    $ dpkg-source -x chromium-embedded-framework_*.dsc
    $ cd chromium-embedded-framework-*/
    $ dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc

Build requirements:
  - 40 GB disk space
  - 8 GB RAM minimum (16+ GB recommended)
  - Build time: 2-7 hours depending on hardware

The build system automatically limits parallelism based on available RAM
to prevent OOM conditions. See debian/README.source for details.

Packages Enabled
----------------

This CEF package enables functionality in:

  - obs-studio: Browser sources (currently disabled with -DENABLE_BROWSER=FALSE)
  - stremio-gtk: Entire application (currently cannot be packaged)
  - casparcg-server: HTTP support (currently disabled)
  - nageru: Potential improvements (to be investigated)

These packages have been waiting for CEF since 2018 (bug #915400).

Runtime Libraries and Configuration
-----------------------------------

**ANGLE Libraries (libEGL.so, libGLESv2.so):**

CEF includes Google's ANGLE libraries (Almost Native Graphics Layer Engine),
which provide OpenGL ES implementation over Vulkan. These are NOT the same
as system Mesa libraries (libegl1, libgles2).

To avoid conflicts with system Mesa libraries, the ANGLE libraries are
installed to a private directory:

  /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/cef/

The main CEF library (libcef.so) has RUNPATH set to find these libraries
automatically. This follows Debian policy for private shared libraries:

  https://wiki.debian.org/RpathIssue

Applications using CEF will automatically use the correct ANGLE libraries
without needing to set LD_LIBRARY_PATH.

**Chrome Sandbox:**

CEF reuses Debian's chromium-sandbox package for process isolation. A symlink
at /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/chrome-sandbox points to /usr/lib/chromium/chrome-sandbox
(which has the required SUID 4755 permissions).

On modern kernels with unprivileged user namespaces, the namespace sandbox is
preferred and the SUID sandbox serves as a fallback.

**SwiftShader (Software Rendering):**

CEF includes SwiftShader for software Vulkan rendering when hardware
acceleration is unavailable. The Vulkan ICD configuration is installed to:

  /usr/share/vulkan/icd.d/vk_swiftshader_icd.json

**FFmpeg Codec Support:**

CEF is built with is_component_ffmpeg=true, which means it dynamically loads
the system's libffmpeg.so for media codec support. This enables:

  - H.264/AVC video decoding (when libavcodec-extra is installed)
  - AAC audio decoding (when libavcodec-extra is installed)
  - Other codecs supported by FFmpeg

The package declares: Depends: libavcodec-extra | libavcodec61

For full media playback support (e.g., streaming services), install:

  sudo apt install libavcodec-extra

**Resource Files:**

CEF resource files (PAK files, locales, ICU data) are in the cef-common
package, installed to:

  /usr/share/cef/

Applications need to set CefSettings.resources_dir_path to this location,
or symlink these files to the application's working directory.

CEF and Chromium Version Alignment
----------------------------------

CEF uses its own version numbering that is DISTINCT from the Chromium version.
The relationship is:

  CEF Version    CEF Branch    Chromium Version     Debian Status
  -----------    ----------    ----------------     -------------
  CEF 138        7499          143.0.7499.x         previous
  CEF 145        7632          145.0.7632.x         current (145.0.7632.75)

**Why This Matters:**

This package (libcef145) was chosen specifically to align with Debian Chromium
in testing (145.0.7632.75). The CEF branch number (7632) corresponds to the
Chromium build number (145.0.**7632**.x).

**CEF Version Scheme:**

  - CEF version number (e.g., 145) is the CEF project's own major version
  - CEF branch number (e.g., 7632) maps directly to Chromium build number
  - Chromium version format: MAJOR.MINOR.BUILD.PATCH (e.g., 145.0.7632.75)
  - CEF branch 7632 = Chromium 145.0.7632.x

**Upstream CEF Source:**

  - Upstream URL: https://bitbucket.org/chromiumembedded/cef
  - Branch: 7632 (CEF 145)
  - CEF expects: refs/tags/145.0.7632.75
  - Debian Chromium provides: 145.0.7632.75

Note: CEF specifies the exact Chromium tag it was developed against.
For this release, CEF and Debian Chromium versions match exactly.

Future Migration: Debian Package Dependencies
----------------------------------------------

The MUT tarballs are an interim solution. When Debian provides the following
packages, this source package will be updated to use them as Build-Depends:

**chromium-source (Bug #893448):**

When the Debian Chromium team provides a chromium-source binary package:

  - Remove orig-chromium.tar.xz from MUT
  - Add Build-Depends: chromium-source
  - Update debian/rules to copy from /usr/src/chromium/
  - Benefits: Automatic security updates, reduced source package size

**depot-tools (hypothetical):**

If a depot-tools Debian package is ever created:

  - Remove orig-depot-tools.tar.xz from MUT
  - Add Build-Depends: depot-tools
  - Benefits: Shared maintenance, automatic updates

**rust-src:**

Debian rust-src 1.91.1+ now provides all files Chromium's build system requires
(including sync/nonpoison/condvar.rs, rwlock.rs). The build uses system rust-src
via Build-Depends: rust-src. No bundled Rust tarball is needed.

The packaging has been designed to make these migrations straightforward.
See debian/README.source for implementation details.

Security Updates
----------------

CEF inherits its security posture from the Chromium version it is built against.
Security updates are delivered by rebuilding CEF against the latest Debian
Chromium source package. When the chromium-source binary package becomes
available (bug #893448), this process will be simplified to a Build-Depends
version bump.

